>
  <p>
    Burst pipe water damage in Baytown tends to arrive in one of two ways: all at once during a rare hard freeze, when half the street has the same problem, or quietly on a normal weekday when a hose behind the washing machine lets go. Either way the first ten minutes matter most. This page covers those minutes, then the repair and cleanup that follow.
  </p>

  <h2>First steps for burst pipe water damage in Baytown homes</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Shut off the water.</strong> Use the fixture valve if the leak is at a toilet, sink or appliance. Otherwise close the main valve at the house or at the meter box near the street.</li>
    <li><strong>Cut power to wet areas if you can do it safely.</strong> If water is near outlets, cords or the breaker panel, or you would have to stand in water to reach the panel, stay back and call your electric utility or an electrician.</li>
    <li><strong>Open a faucet at the lowest point of the house</strong> to drain what is left in the lines and take pressure off the break.</li>
    <li><strong>If the water heater is the source,</strong> close the cold water valve above the tank and turn off the gas control or the breaker for the heater.</li>
    <li><strong>Take photos and video</strong> of the break, the water and everything it touched before you move things.</li>
    <li><strong>Move what you can.</strong> Lift furniture legs onto blocks or foil, pick up rugs, and carry electronics, papers and valuables to a dry room.</li>
    <li><strong>Watch the ceiling.</strong> A sagging, bulging ceiling is holding water and can fall. Keep everyone out from under it.</li>
    <li><strong>Call a licensed plumber for the pipe and a restoration company for the water.</strong> Then call your insurer.</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="disclosure">
    <p><strong>What our number does:</strong> it routes you to an independent restoration company for water removal and drying. That company may or may not have a plumber on staff. Ask when you are connected.</p>
  </div>

